PART 12 – AUTOMATIC AI API KEY AND PROVIDER FAILOVER

My existing project already has multiple API keys and AI providers connected.

The system currently requires me to switch manually when a key reaches its limit or encounters an error.

I do NOT want a replacement AI system.

I want the existing system improved.

Required behavior

Suppose I have multiple API keys:

API 1 → API 2 → API 3 → API 4 → API 5.

If API 1 fails or reaches its quota:

- Automatically identify the failure.
- Mark the key temporarily unavailable when appropriate.
- Activate the next available key.
- Continue processing the request safely.

If API 2 fails, move to API 3.

Continue until an available compatible provider is found.

Failover requirements

Handle:

- Quota exhaustion.
- Rate limits.
- Temporary provider outages.
- Authentication failures.
- Network failures.
- Timeout errors.
- Provider-specific errors.

Additional requirements:

- No manual switching.
- No unnecessary duplicate requests.
- Safe retry logic.
- Exponential backoff where appropriate.
- Provider health tracking.
- Recovery of temporarily unavailable keys.
- Secure server-side API key storage.
- Error logging without exposing secrets.
- Preserve existing model and provider configurations.

Do not retry a failed payment-related or other non-idempotent action in a way that causes duplicate operations.

If all configured AI providers fail, show a clear temporary service error.

Never expose API keys in browser JavaScript, HTML, network responses, or user-facing logs.

